  "body": "In https://github.com/whatwg/streams/issues/241#issuecomment-68834017 @tyoshino proposed making a stream reader look \"closed\" once it is released. Right now it just passes through `ready`/`state`/`closed` to the underlying stream, although `read()` and `cancel()` fail.\n\nThere's no immediately-convincing argument for one over the other, but after some thought I think the \"closed\" is better. It means that more invariants that apply to streams (e.g., if state is \"readable\", you can call read() successfully) will apply to readers. And it allows you to pass the reader object to someone without them having to think about whether it's been released or not, as long as they are equipped to handle closed streams.\n",
